# Sample data artifacts
*.csv
*.json
*.bpmn
*.zip
# BPS models are the experimental apparatus, not build output: the blanket
# *.json / *.bpmn rules above would otherwise leave every model a paper's
# results depend on untracked, while tracking the .csv.gz logs that go with
# them -- a clone would get the logs and not the models, and the evaluation
# pipelines would not run. Generator scripts live in tools/generate_*.py, but
# they are unseeded, so re-running them does NOT reproduce these exact files.
!samples/**/*.bpmn
!samples/**/*.json

# The reference grid the harness compares a fresh run against, and the
# simulation logs it was computed from. Prosimos is seeded but not fully
# deterministic, so a fresh run cannot reproduce the published cells exactly --
# only these logs can, which is why they are tracked. They are gzipped: 909 MB
# of CSV, 161 MB on disk. The blanket *.csv / *.json rules above must not
# swallow either.
!evaluation/state_metrics/reference_results.csv
!evaluation/state_metrics/reference_runs/**

# Paper sources and working notes. The LaTeX, the figures and the running
# commentary are drafted outside this repository; what a reader needs to
# reproduce the numbers is the code, run_evaluation.sh and the reference grid.
# The scenario catalogues under evaluation/state_metrics/ are design notes from
# the same drafting: they record what was considered, not what the harness runs,
# and datasets.py / perturb.py are the authority on that.
/paper/
/docs/
evaluation/state_metrics/*.md

# Loose working files at the root -- run logs, half-finished notes, one-off
# scripts. Anything worth keeping earns a real name under evaluation/ or tools/.
/scratch_*
/.codex

!package.json
!package-lock.json
!tsconfig.json
!pyproject.toml
